Three fixes for the A10/A20 display frontend, found while playing
cedrus-decoded H.264 video on an overlay plane on a Cubietruck (A20) at
1080p60.

1/3 programs the start address and in-tile offsets of cropped tiled
    (MB32) sources, which were read from the wrong tiles whenever the
    source did not start at (0,0), e.g. when a video player crops the
    source of a window that is partly off the screen.
2/3 picks the scaler filters by the scaling ratio, as the Allwinner BSP
    does, instead of one fixed set without low-pass; any downscaled
    plane aliased. The coefficient table comes from the GPL-licensed
    linux-sunxi 3.4 BSP kernel; the commit message gives the source.
3/3 skips every other input line when a plane would need more than
    the frontend can read per output line (measured: a pixel rate and
    a DRAM bandwidth limit, budgets derived from the CRTC mode), and
    rejects planes that exceed it even so; before, the whole screen
    got corrupted.

2/3 and 3/3 only change the A10/A20 frontend (new quirk flags); the
A23/A33 frontend keeps its fixed filter and its behaviour. 1/3 changes
the tiled two-plane path of every frontend this driver handles; it was
only tested on the A20.

1/3 is a plain fix (Fixes: tag) and does not depend on the other two;
it can be taken on its own through the fixes tree. 3/3 builds on it.

Testing: 1/3 on a Cubieboard2 (A20) with Armbian's 6.18.56 using
synthetic tiled NV12 test pictures, 2/3 and 3/3 together on a
Cubietruck (A20) with 6.18.56 and cedrus-decoded tiled NV12 video
(1080p60 HDMI, single head; the player side was our own VDPAU driver,
which is not public yet) and modetest with linear XRGB8888 on an
overlay plane, which gave the throughput budgets of 3/3. Those tests
ran an earlier 3/3 that skipped lines beyond a plain ratio of 2; this
version: tested (XR24 overlay 0.75..0.333 stable, 0.30..0.25 refused; VDPAU NV12
1280x720..480x270 correct, smaller refused). Other display modes, dual head and the A10 were not
tested, and the v7.3-rc7 versions were build-tested (W=1, each patch)
but not booted.

3/3's budgets (260 Mpixels/s, 0.8 GB/s) come from measurements on one
board at one DRAM clock with one head; they do not account for a slower
DRAM or a second head's scanout. Opinions on a better model welcome.

The patches were written with an AI assistant; I reviewed and tested
them.

D.R.racer (3):
  drm/sun4i: frontend: honour the source offset of tiled semi-planar
    buffers
  drm/sun4i: frontend: select the scaler filter by scaling ratio
  drm/sun4i: frontend: skip input lines to stay within its throughput

